id: pm-sy24w2
title: "GH-930: duplicates --status all silently scans zero items"
description: Core duplicates accepts the natural all-status sentinel as a literal status and returns a false-clean zero-item scan instead of inspecting all lifecycle states or refusing invalid input.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-07T19:42:18.033Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-08T16:50:02.969Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-08T16:50:02.492Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-08T16:50:02.492Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Core duplicates treats --status all as explicit no restriction with candidate-count parity to an omitted filter; configured status validation still rejects unknown values; structured cost and filter receipts expose the effective selection; CLI SDK contracts docs and negative tests prevent another false-clean zero-scan regression.
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.7 with project extensions enabled or disabled
repro_steps: Compare pm duplicates --status all --threshold 0.82 --limit 100 with the same command omitting --status; the former reports cost.item_count=0 while the latter reports the full tracker count.
resolution: fixed
expected_result: Explicit all-status duplicate scans inspect the same complete lifecycle corpus as the unfiltered command and cannot silently degrade to zero candidates.
actual_result: "The duplicate-analysis SDK and CLI now normalize and validate lifecycle status filters at runtime, treat status=all as an unrestricted corpus, and emit the applied bounded filters in the result contract."
customer_impact: Agents receive an exit-0 false-clean duplicate audit and can create duplicate work despite following the required all-status workflow.
